<%# ICODOS override of notifications_settings/_reminder_banner.html.erb
    Upstream renders the "unlock with DocuSeal Pro" upsell, which does not apply
    here.

    RENDERS NOTHING WHEN ALL IS WELL. Counts, "last checked" and other status
    were removed on request: they are noise on a settings page, and the numbers
    change on their own so they read as clutter rather than information.

    What remains are the states in which reminders are NOT reaching anyone,
    split by whether somebody chose that or it broke:

      red    something is wrong and nobody decided it
               - the status probe itself failed
               - the scheduler has stalled, which is the exact failure this
                 feature exists to prevent (looks switched on, quietly stopped)
      amber  switched off deliberately, on the server, not on this page
               - test mode: the schedule is worked out but no email is sent
               - reminders disabled outright

    The colour is a chip background rather than coloured text: coloured text at
    these weights fails contrast on the light theme, and the four messages
    already read differently enough to stand on their own without it.

    ONLY USE TAILWIND/DAISYUI CLASSES DOCUSEAL ALREADY USES SOMEWHERE. The CSS in
    /app/public/packs is precompiled and Tailwind purged the rest, so an unused
    class silently does nothing — no error, just wrong layout. gap-x-6, gap-x-3,
    alert-error, alert-warning, md:join-horizontal and leading-snug are absent.
    Verify before using:
      grep -F 'the-class' /app/public/packs/css/application-*.css

    CHECK ON EVERY DOCUSEAL VERSION BUMP — a stale override renders silently.
%>
<% status = IcodosReminderSweep.status(current_account) rescue { error: 'unavailable' } %>

<%
  severity, message =
    if status[:error]
      ['broken', "Reminder status is unavailable: #{status[:error]}"]
    elsif status[:enabled] && status[:dry_run]
      ['chosen', 'Test mode: reminders are worked out but no email is actually sent.']
    elsif status[:enabled] && status[:stale]
      ['broken', 'Nothing has been checked for over two hours, so reminders are not going out. ' \
                 'The scheduled task on the server has probably stopped.']
    elsif !status[:enabled]
      ['chosen', 'Reminders are switched off on the server, so nobody is being chased.']
    end
%>

<% if message %>
  <p class="mt-2 mb-2 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium <%= severity == 'broken' ? 'bg-red-100' : 'bg-yellow-100' %>">
    <%= message %>
  </p>
<% end %>
